ngm:layer-2-security-council a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Layer 2 Security Council"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A Layer 2 Security Council is a designated multi-signature governance body empowered to take privileged actions on a Layer 2 rollup, such as pausing the bridge, executing emergency upgrades, or resolving stuck states during the maturation period before fully trustless operation. It typically comprises a quorum of independent signers from distinct organisations to mitigate single-party capture. The construct trades some decentralisation for the ability to respond rapidly to critical vulnerabilities."@en ;
