ngm:liverpool-smart-cities a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Liverpool Smart Cities"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Liverpool Smart Cities refers to the Merseyside city region's integrated programme of digital innovation, IoT deployment, and sustainable urban infrastructure targeting net-zero carbon status by 2030 and 100,000 new jobs by 2040. It encompasses city council strategy, university-led research (University of Liverpool, LJMU, Edge Hill), the Horizons innovation programme backed by the UK Shared Prosperity Fund, and partnerships driving smart transport, digital health, and climate technology."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
