ngm:goal-specification a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Goal Specification"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Goal specification is the formal description of what an autonomous agent or planner is meant to achieve, expressed as target states, conditions, objectives, or reward functions. It translates high-level intent into a representation that planning and reasoning systems can evaluate and pursue. Clear goal specification is essential for task planning and avoiding misaligned or unsafe agent behaviour."@en ;
