ngm:decision-tree a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Decision Tree"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "A decision tree is a supervised learning model that predicts an outcome by recursively partitioning the feature space into regions, represented as a tree of decision nodes and leaf nodes. Each internal node tests a feature against a threshold and routes an instance down a branch, while leaves assign a class label or numeric value. Decision trees are valued for their interpretability and form the building blocks of ensemble methods such as random forests and gradient boosting."@en ;
